Maybe they will in the next version. (A non-trivial number of players
stopped caring about the scorefile long ago, since the scoring algorithm
is only really any good for comparing *losing* games and even then can
be gamed into meaninglessness; see also the public-server games where
people managed to achieve a score of INT_MAX by boulderfarming one of
the Riders.)

Also, of course:
 - *all* your games are recorded in the logfile.
 - PERSMAX is the number of high scores kept in 'record' per role/name
   combination (or per role/UID combination if PERS_IS_UID is defined).

>Seriously just check the directory in which the executable resides for
>the config file and allow special options there. This kind of problem
>really sucks.

In the meantime, this wouldn't be too hard to write a patch to address.
